    q: 'We only use ChatGPT internally. Do we have obligations?',
    a: 'Yes, but reasonable ones. You are not an AI provider but a deployer, and the AI literacy obligation has applied since 2 February 2025: staff working with AI systems must have a sufficient level of competence. In practice this means an internal usage policy (what data must never be entered, how outputs are checked) and documented basic training.',
  },
  {
    q: 'We have a chatbot on our website. What do we need to do?',
    a: 'From 2 August 2026 the transparency obligations in Art. 50 apply: users must be clearly informed they are interacting with an AI system, and generated content must be marked. A visible notice in the chat interface usually covers the disclosure part. For systems already on the market before 2 August 2026, machine-readable marking of generated content has a deadline of 2 December 2026.',
  },
  {
    q: 'We use AI to screen CVs. Is that a high-risk system?',
    a: 'Yes — recruitment and employment decisions are in Annex III, the high-risk category. The deadline for full obligations was postponed to 2 December 2027 by the Digital Omnibus regulation, but vendor selection and process documentation are worth starting now: replacing a tool a few months before the deadline is far more expensive than choosing correctly in the first place.',
  },
  {
    q: 'The high-risk deadline was postponed. Can we postpone too?',
    a: 'No, because the postponement did not touch the block that already applies. The prohibitions and AI literacy have applied since February 2025, the GPAI rules since August 2025, and transparency from August 2026. Only the hardest part — high-risk systems — moved, and only for organisations that have such systems.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What penalties does a company face?',
    a: 'Up to EUR 35 million or 7% of total worldwide annual turnover for prohibited practices, and up to EUR 15 million or 3% for breaching other obligations — whichever is higher. For SMEs and start-ups the rule is inverted: the lower of the two caps applies.',
